--// SECTION 33 — FREQUENTLY ASKED QUESTIONS
--================================================================================
--[[
	Q: Does this work on mobile?
	A: Yes. Touch drag, touch resize, touch sliders/dropdowns all work.
	   Sidebar auto-collapses to icon rail. UIScale auto-fits to screen.

	Q: Can I use this in my own game / script hub?
	A: Yes, free for personal and commercial use. Keep the header credit.

	Q: How do I change the default theme?
	A: Pass Palette = 2 (or 1..10) to CreateWindow, or call win:SetPalette(n).

	Q: The window is too big/small.
	A: Set CONFIG.WindowWidth/Height before CreateWindow, or drag the
	   bottom-right corner to resize. Auto-scale handles the rest.

	Q: I want to remove the aurora background blobs.
	A: Set ShowBackground = false (default) — blobs only show when true.
	   They live in win.Background; set .Visible = false to hide.

	Q: Notifications don't appear.
	A: Ensure you call win:Notify() on a Window object, not Aurora.
	   Check DisplayOrder if other GUIs overlap.

	Q: How do I add my own icons?
	A: Upload a 1:1 transparent PNG, copy its asset id, add to ICONS table
	   at the top: myicon = "rbxassetid://1234567890".

	Q: Can I have multiple toggles in one row?
	A: Use a Card or Grid container and parent smaller custom frames,
	   or use AddSegmented / AddRadioGroup for grouped selection.

	Q: Does it lag?
	A: Each drifting gradient uses one RenderStepped connection. With
	   typical usage (< 30 animated elements) impact is negligible.
	   Anim.Cleanup() disconnects everything on window destroy.

	Q: How do I make my own component?
	A: Use Aurora.Utils.New() + Aurora.Utils.Corner/Stroke/Gradient helpers,
	   parent into a Tab page or Card.Content, and use Anim.ApplyHover for
	   the standard hover feel.
]]

